{title: Like Incense Sometimes}
{artist: Hillsong Worship}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Verse 1}
May my [C]prayer like incense rise before You
The [Am]lifting of my hands a sacrifice
[F]Oh Lord Jesus turn Your eyes upon me
For I [Dm]know there is mercy in Your [G]sight
Your [C]statues are my heritage forever
My [Am]heart is set on keeping Your decrees
Please[F] still my anxious urge toward rebellion
[Dm]Let love keep my will [G]upon its knees

{comment: Chorus}
Oh [C]God, You are my [G]God
And I [F]will ever praise [C]You

{comment: Verse 2}
To [C]all creation I can see a limit
But [Am]Your commands are boundless and have none
So Your [F]word is my joy and meditation
From the [Dm]rising to the setting of [G]the sun
[C]All Your ways are loving and are faithful
Your [Am]road is narrow but Your burden light
[F]Because You gladly lean to lead the humble
[Dm]I shall gladly kneel to leave [G]my pride
